Coreference resolution (coref)

This project includes code adapted from the Google Research project "coref_mt5"
(https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/coref_mt5),
Copyright 2022 The Google Research Authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  - src/coref/coreference.py (adapted from colabs/coreference_decoder.ipynb)

tools/convert_checkpoint.py is a memory-efficient replacement for Hugging Face's
convert_t5x_checkpoint_to_pytorch.py (Apache License, Version 2.0).

The method is described in:
  Bohnet, Alberti, Collins (2023). "Coreference Resolution through a seq2seq Transition-Based System."
  Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics. https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.12142

The pre-trained model checkpoint is not part of this repository. It is provided by Google Research
(see the link in the README) and is subject to the terms under which it is distributed there.
